# Hub surface nesting (subtle contrast only)

When placing a box, card, or container **inside** another panel, give it a **slightly** different background and a **discrete** border so it does not merge with the parent. Do **not** redesign typography, sizing, or layout when only contrast was requested.

## Tokens (`src/lib/hub/shellTokens.ts`)

| Layer | Token | Intent |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Panel | `KX_PANEL`, `KX_FORM_PANEL`, aside chrome | `white` / `zinc-900` |
| Nested box | `KX_SURFACE_NESTED`, `KX_METADATA_STAT_CARD`, `KX_SURFACE_INSET`, `KX_SURFACE_ROW` | Subtle lift: `zinc-50` + soft border / dark `white/[0.04]` + `zinc-800` border |

## Metadata / stat boxes

**Locked.** See `.cursor/rules/hub-metadata-stat-boxes.mdc`. Always `HubMetadataStatGrid` / `HubMetadataStatCard` (or `TokenStatCard` alias). Equal height, `gap-3`, max 3 per row.

## Rules

1. Nested bg must differ from parent, but **not harshly** (avoid jumping to hard `zinc-800` bricks on `zinc-900` panels).
2. Borders stay soft (`zinc-200/80`, `zinc-800`), not high-contrast outlines.
3. Prefer shared tokens; do not invent one-off nested backgrounds.
4. Fixing merge contrast is **not** permission to restyle the whole card.
